5d:T1261,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What exactly do I get for one placement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A brand-new article published on someone else's blog, with a 250-350 word section about you inside it - your site shown alongside it, and exactly 1 link to the page you chose. Not a line squeezed into an old post, and not a sponsored box at the bottom."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pick the sites myself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, and that is the point - there is no catalogue to trawl through. Every day we look for blogs that earn real Google traffic in your subject and publish in your language, score them for fit, and place you on the best one you can afford. What you control is the floor: Domain Rating 30 up to 70, which pages get linked, and how many credits a month you are willing to spend."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who writes the article, and can I change it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do - the article is AI-written for the host blog, in that blogâ€™s own voice, and nobody sends you a brief to fill in. Before it publishes you can read it, edit the title, body and meta description, ask AI to rewrite it, or regenerate the whole thing. Once it is live it belongs to the host blog."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does a link cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The host's Domain Rating times 4 credits. A DR 60 blog costs 240 credits, a DR 30 one costs 120. It all runs on the Scale backlink plan, which carries 1,400 credits a month at $899, and you can cap how much of that goes on placements."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many links will I get in a month?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As many as your credits and your standards allow - but we will not promise you a number. A placement only happens when a blog genuinely fits: same language, above your Domain Rating floor, pulling real traffic in your subject, and not one you already hold a live link on. In a narrow niche some days pass with no match at all, and we would rather skip a day than put you on a blog that has nothing to do with you. A quiet month is not a wasted one: credits you do not spend stay on your balance and the next month's are added on top."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if the link is removed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We re-check every live link every 2 days for 90 days. If yours disappears, the publisher is notified and has 7 days to restore it. If it does not come back, the placement is marked lost, your credits are returned automatically, and that page goes back in the queue to be placed somewhere else for no more than it originally cost. Credits also come back if the publisher declines, if the article fails to generate, if publishing stalls, or if the link never verifies within 21 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are the links dofollow?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. They go in as ordinary editorial links in the body of the article - we never add a nofollow attribute. Every re-check records whether the link is still dofollow, and a publisher whose link turns to nofollow hears about it from us. What nobody can honestly promise is what any given link does for your rankings - anyone quoting you a number is guessing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What kind of sites are they?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Real blogs with real traffic: Domain Rating 30+, around 100 organic clicks from Google a month, Google Search Console connected with 3+ months of history, on their own domain, with a working CMS connection. A site that slips below the bar stops receiving placements."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this the kind of link building that gets sites penalised?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nobody outside Google can promise you an answer to that, and you should distrust anyone who does. What we can tell you is how these placements are built: one link per article, inside a full piece written for that blog's own readers, on a topic cleared against what the blog already ranks for, on sites with real Google traffic rather than networks built to sell links. No link farms, no site-wide footers, no bundles of cheap links. You also control the pace - your monthly budget caps how fast links appear."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I control the anchor text?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Each of your 10 target pages can carry up to 5 anchors of up to 65 characters, and one of them is used word for word. Leave them blank and the writer picks a phrase that reads naturally in the sentence it sits in."}}]}2d:["$","section",null,{"className":"section ","id":"faq","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$5d"}}]],"$L5e"]}]
